From 59e75c8cc82b6c80b64e693d3316d3739b304656 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:36:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop cancel() reaching a section that has gone

Each module publishes its running section in m_currentSection so that
cancel(), called from the host's thread, can stop it. The section
lives in a block (or a switch case) inside execute(), but the pointer
was cleared only after that block ended, so a Cancel arriving as the
section finished called cancel() on a destroyed object. Under ASan
this is a stack-use-after-scope in LinkModule::cancel, reached by
SetMode 0x10 and Cancel in a loop; on hardware it is a call through
whatever has since been written to that stack slot.

Publish, re-check m_cancel and clear the pointer under irq_lock, and
clear it before the section is destroyed; cancel() takes the same
lock, so the section cannot go while it is being cancelled. Every
section's cancel() only sets flags or gives semaphores, so nothing
blocks under the lock. Applies to the GBA link, Advance Wars, Battle
Chip Gate, e-Reader, trade emulator and Wireless Adapter modules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014LvpUYFw94JkaNFyrbwJmK
